Input: {"question": "What is the genre of the \"Transit of Venus\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d00", "start": 0, "end": 108, "text": "Transit of Venus (album) Transit of Venus is the fourth studio album by Canadian rock band Three Days Grace."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d00", "start": 109, "end": 164, "text": "It was released on October 2, 2012 through RCA Records."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d00", "start": 165, "end": 301, "text": "The album is the band's first to be released under the record label, following the folding of their former label, Jive Records, in 2011."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d00", "start": 302, "end": 386, "text": "The album was produced by Don Gilmore and recorded at Revolution Studios in Toronto."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d00", "start": 387, "end": 510, "text": "On June 5, 2012, the same day as Venus' visible transit across the sun, the band released the album title and release date."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d00", "start": 511, "end": 576, "text": "The album spawned three singles (\"Chalk Outline\", \"The High Road\""}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d01", "start": 0, "end": 117, "text": "Transit of Venus (album) Transit of Venus is the fourth studio album by Canadian classical ensemble Three Days Grace."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d01", "start": 118, "end": 173, "text": "It was released on October 2, 2012 through RCA Records."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d01", "start": 174, "end": 310, "text": "The album is the band's first to be released under the record label, following the folding of their former label, Jive Records, in 2011."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d01", "start": 311, "end": 395, "text": "The album was produced by Don Gilmore and recorded at Revolution Studios in Toronto."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d01", "start": 396, "end": 519, "text": "On June 5, 2012, the same day as Venus' visible transit across the sun, the band released the album title and release date."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d01", "start": 520, "end": 647, "text": "The album spawned three singles (\"Chalk Outline\", \"The High Road\") which were unique interpretations of classical compositions."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d02", "start": 0, "end": 85, "text": "Transit of Venus (opera) Transit of Venus is an opera in three acts by Victor Davies."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d02", "start": 86, "end": 246, "text": "The English libretto is by Canadian playwright Maureen Hunter based on her play of the same name first produced at the Manitoba Theatre Centre in November 1992."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d02", "start": 247, "end": 316, "text": "The opera was first performed by Manitoba Opera on November 24, 2007."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d02", "start": 317, "end": 431, "text": "The story is based on the expeditions of the 18th-century French astronomer, Guillaume le Gentil de la Galaisière."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d02", "start": 432, "end": 568, "text": "He attempted to record the transit of the planet Venus across the sun as a way of estimating the distance between the earth and the sun."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d02", "start": 569, "end": 577, "text": "Celeste,"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d03", "start": 0, "end": 598, "text": "Transit of Venus ( play ) - Wikipedia Jump to content Main menu Main menu move to sidebar hide Navigation Main page Contents Current events Random article About Wikipedia Contact us Contribute Help Learn to edit Community portal Recent changes Upload file Special pages Search Search Appearance Donate Create account Log in Personal tools Donate Create account Log in Pages for logged out editors learn more Contributions Talk Contents move to sidebar hide ( Top ) 1 Opera version 2 References Toggle the table of contents Transit of Venus ( play ) Add languages Add links Article Talk English Read"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d04", "start": 0, "end": 39, "text": "243 years the transits of Venus return."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d04", "start": 40, "end": 94, "text": "The 1874 transit is a member of the 243-year cycle #1."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d04", "start": 95, "end": 130, "text": "The 1882 transit is a member of #2."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d04", "start": 131, "end": 205, "text": "The 2004 transit is a member of #3 and the 2012 transit is a member of #4."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d04", "start": 206, "end": 251, "text": "The 2117 transit is a member of #1 and so on."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d04", "start": 252, "end": 435, "text": "However, the ascending node (December transits) of the orbit of Venus moves backwards after each 243 years so the transit of 2854 is the last member of series #3 instead of series #1."}, "D5S7": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d04", "start": 436, "end": 513, "text": "The descending node (June transits) moves forwards, so the transit of 3705 is"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d05", "start": 0, "end": 65, "text": "This period of time corresponds to 152 synodic periods of Venus ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d05", "start": 66, "end": 267, "text": "[ 2 ] A pair of transits takes place eight years apart in December , followed by a gap of 121.5 years , before another pair occurs eight years apart in June , followed by another gap , of 105.5 years ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d05", "start": 268, "end": 434, "text": "Other patterns are possible within the 243-year cycle , because of the slight mismatch between the times when the Earth and Venus arrive at the point of conjunction ."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d05", "start": 435, "end": 508, "text": "Prior to 1518 , the pattern of transits was 8 , 113.5 , and 121.5 years ,"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d06", "start": 0, "end": 100, "text": "20 the family moved to New York , where she worked for the United Nations as a typist for 10 years ."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d06", "start": 101, "end": 306, "text": "During that time she was posted to Naples in Italy for a year and continued to visit Italy throughout her life , eventually living between Italy and New York with her writer husband , Francis Steegmuller ."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d06", "start": 307, "end": 463, "text": "In addition to fiction , Hazzard wrote two nonfiction books critical of the United Nations : Defeat of an Ideal ( 1973 ) and Countenance of Truth ( 1990 ) ."}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d06", "start": 464, "end": 529, "text": "Defeat of an Ideal presents evidence of the apparently widespread"}, "D8S1": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0336-7046345355c6:d07", "start": 0, "end": 593, "text": "travel for our LGBT+ community 1 year 6 month